# React 19 & R3F

## Components
- ONLY functional components. No class components.
- `ref` as a normal prop (no `forwardRef` – not needed in React 19).
- `use()` to consume promises/context where it fits.
- Actions + `useActionState` / `useOptimistic` for forms/mutations.
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks (`useXxx`).

## Rendering performance
- `useMemo` for heavy work; `useCallback` only when children are memoized.
- Avoid inline object literals as props to memoized children.

## R3F
- No allocation in `useFrame` – reuse `Vector3`/`Quaternion` instances outside the loop.
- **Scratch ownership:** singleton scene hooks (one mount per canvas) may use module-level scratch vectors. Multi-instance components (`map` over bodies, labels, etc.) must use `useRef(new Vector3())` per instance so parallel `useFrame` callbacks do not clobber shared state.
- Prefer `out` parameters in math helpers when the caller already owns the buffer.
- `useGLTF` / `useTexture` for assets; call `.preload()` where appropriate.
- Use `<Instances>` for many identical meshes.
- Prefer `<Suspense>` + drei loaders over manual loading.
